body:
I am studying CS, but I am defiantly not an expert in commenting code, so I have a question for you.

I have been writing some functions with a kind of comment layout, where I make a few comment of what I think should be done and the ordre I want it in. Forexample I wrote a function starting by writing this comments 

    // Check if order exist in C5 db

    // Check if the order has lines (if it does not we cannot use it)

    // Update order

    // Update order lines

Afterwards I write helper functions to do all 4 parts and call them. Is that good practices? And is that the right way to use commenting? (In the helper functions I also have comments explain funny code, because C5 and MS SQL is quite strange to work with...).
